Why Am I Making This?

I have a little project notebook where I write notes and measurements that seems to work well for what I need while modeling. And I already have all files on my Google Drive. So in many respects tracking this project in a repo seems pointless.

I'm also thus far writing this like a blog or How to (or "How I"?) thing, which I don't think is condusive to this project's development. By my nature I like to hear myself talk and imagine someone out there could be entertained. (notice meeeee)

But I think primarily I'd like to start a practice of using a git for my own projects in some way, so here we are. It's a start. And it would feel even more overkill to start up a Jira page but maybe I'll do that for something I think I might work on with a buddy.

Regardless, going through the motions of using this to learn habits on a little project of my own without consequence. Plus, your boi loves him some LEGACY so it'd be really cool to look back at this in a few years and hopefully have many more projects in my "portfolio" by then.
